  "live_records": {
    "q-36467": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36467",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=0$ gives two lines\n\nII. $c=1$ gives a circle\n\nIII. $c=2$ gives a hyperbola",
      "worked_solution": "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0$ the level curves are $y=\\pm 2x,$ which consists of two lines.\n\n- If $c=1$ the level curve is $4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=1,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ the level curve is $2{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\nSo, only statements I and III are true.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-36467-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and II only",
              "html": "I and II only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-36467-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and III only",
              "html": "I and III only"
            },
            {
              "option": "c",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-36467-c",
